build/
/dev/l2src_sandbox/build*
/dev/**/build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude-bridge/
claude_chat/profiles/
claude_chat/uds_debug.log
claude_chat/latest
claude_chat/.claude/
.claude/worktrees/

# The L1 self-build's C-seed lives at lm1/build.  It is the ONLY thing under a "build/" path that
# must be versioned: without it the self-build cannot even start (B0 = gcc of this C), and a clean
# clone cannot reproduce the fixed point.  Narrow and exact -- this is NOT a general un-ignore of
# build trees; everything else under any build/ stays ignored.  Written down after Codex's audit
# LMX-L1FIXPOINT-AUDIT-20260920-01, which measured that the seed was hidden by the `build/` rule.
!lm1/build/
!lm1/build/**

# Run leftovers of the port's own build script: not sources, and they came over with the copy.
dev/mixa_sandbox/*.pid
dev/mixa_sandbox/*.err
dev/mixa_sandbox/build_mixa_*.txt
dev/mixa_sandbox/**/*.o
# The port STAGES the kernel's .lm1 beside itself so that `predef: "l2src/..."` resolves from the
# CWD (the translator resolves predefs itself; gcc's -I does not enter into it).  The staging is a
# COPY that build_mixa.ps1 recreates whenever it is missing -- so it is never a source, and it must
# never be swept into a commit: 103 files belonging to the kernel line would land under the port's
# name, and the next `git add -A` by anyone would carry them.  Ignored by NAME, not by a blanket
# rule, so the day the staging is replaced by a real resolution this line is the one to delete.
dev/mixa_sandbox/l2src/
# The same script stages the FIXTURE PROGRAMS the process probe starts (section 2b): built binaries
# in the port root, rebuilt on every gate run.
dev/mixa_sandbox/*.exe

dev/vm_jvm/out/

build/vm_jvm/

# Windows stack dumps of a crashed tool (grep.exe.stackdump landed in 2b0a594 by accident; author, 2026-09-25).
*.stackdump
